  "background": "On the round restricted3-metric choose f by the Dirichlet problem Delta f=0, f=-1 on3S2, f=+1 onT2; choose omega the absolute harmonic1-form with period1. Phi=Psi*d(f/(-3))+log2*chi*omega with a commuting flat unitary SU5 Wilson connection.",
  "background_scope": "Existence-defined elliptic boundary problems. Hopf normal signs and omega normal0 preserve the family relative domains. No explicit numerical Higgs metric or complete7D G2 metric is supplied.",
  "domain_comparison": "If all fields keep the punctured absolute domain, H1 neutral candidates survive and H2 has3boundary classes percharacter. If qPsi=0 fields extend through invisible point caps, nonzeroqchi sectors live on a solidtorus and are acyclic. If bothcharges0, the C4 flat bundle can extend across the wire to the closed lens: H1=H2=0. These are different stated domain choices, not an automatic consequence of the Lie algebra.",
